# Citation metadata for YAPSS. GitHub renders this as "Cite this repository", and
# Zenodo reads it for the metadata of each archived release. See
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/ for the schema.
#
# Update `version` and `date-released` at each release (the release checklist
# has the step). The DOI is the Zenodo *concept* DOI, which always resolves to
# the latest archived version; the per-version DOI is on the Zenodo record.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use YAPSS in published work, please cite it using the metadata in this
  file, giving the version you used.
type: software
title: "YAPSS: Yet Another Pseudo-Spectral Solver"
abstract: >-
  A Python library that transcribes multi-phase optimal control problems into
  nonlinear programs by pseudospectral collocation (Legendre-Gauss,
  Legendre-Gauss-Radau, Legendre-Gauss-Lobatto) and solves them with Ipopt. The
  Legendre-Gauss-Radau transcription follows Patterson and Rao (2014); the
  Legendre-Gauss and Legendre-Gauss-Lobatto transcriptions extend their approach.
authors:
